WEBVTT

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:06.790
<i>In the beginning, God created 
the heavens and the earth.</i>

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:11.890
<i>He followed them</i>

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:15.430
<i>with light, waters, and the land.</i>

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:21.980
<i>Then he created the many animals 
that would inhabit it.</i>

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.640
<i>Or... that was the plan.</i>

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.000
<i>It got too tedious, so he outsourced it.</i>

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:34.180
Heaven's Design Team

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:04.360
You, who have been banished
 to the void in shame,

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:08.780
I now remove your shackles.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:12.290
Come forth, spirit of ash!

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.770
What is this? It's so cool!

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:25.390
This is a dragon!

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:26.790
Amazing, huh?

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:30.120
This is the first work 
of a certain designer.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.200
Who did that?! Who summoned that?!

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:33.990
Oh, he already realized.

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:35.050
Of course I did!

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:37.370
Why did you take out an old, failed design?!

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:40.470
And seriously, what was 
that misleading chant?!

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:44.300
Basically, you were just saying, 
"Let's bring out an embarrassing failure!"

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.290
Well, ash is a form of waste.

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:50.810
I-I'm sorry. I was told to read 
this script to set the mood.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:53.690
I mean, it did feel like a 
proper summoning, right?

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:57.320
Yeah, some mood that was. 
And what's with this star thing?

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:58.700
Is it supposed to be a summoning circle?

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:03.440
Oh, this? I was just doodling 
and thought of a new animal.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:06.740
This was a blueprint? 
I'm sorry for stepping all over it!

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:09.090
It's fine. Nothing's decided yet.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.710
So, why did you bring out the dragon, anyway?

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:17.030
Ah, well, God put in an order for something 
that "has no wings, but still flies."

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:21.720
Then Kanamori-san and Kimura-san said 
there was a perfect fit in the rejected files.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.730
That's no good! Put it away already!

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.340
But it's so cool.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:27.230
Yeah!

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:29.360
That's a stain on my record!

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:31.360
A stain?

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.060
Everybody has one, right?

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:37.360
When they're young, they think 
that weird stuff looks good!

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:40.570
My younger self thought the 
dragon design looked super-cool

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:42.740
and began obsessing over it, 
only to have it be rejected.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:47.620
Put it away already. My inner 
younger self is screaming in pain.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:48.630
Don't you feel bad?

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:50.510
I-It's that bad?

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:55.150
But even though it didn't pass last time, 
maybe we can make it happen this time.

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:57.500
Yeah, think of it as a test of our skills.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:59.890
You're enjoying doing this to me.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:03.210
You guys have your own shameful stains!

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:05.200
How can we make this happen?

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:07.880
Making it fly without wings sounds hard.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:10.770
Anyway, I'll put this dragon away for now.

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:17.010
How about making it float like a balloon?

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:20.670
Then we'd have to fill it with 
something lighter than air.

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:23.640
How about helium? That's light.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:27.030
<b>Helium</b>

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:27.030
<b>Air</b>

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:27.030
Oh, that's the gas that changes 
your voice at parties.

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:29.870
You say that so casually, 
but you'd need something like

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:32.280
nuclear fusion happening in the 
body to produce helium.

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:34.820
If it's about being light, 
wouldn't hydrogen work?

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:38.030
That's good. Hydrogen makes balloons float, too.

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:41.090
Also, microbes in the intestine 
can produce hydrogen

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:42.790
by fermenting food.

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:45.960
So you want to make the 
dragon float with farts?

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:51.460
But in order to produces enough 
gas to make its entire body float,

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:53.890
the animal would have to eat a ton of food.

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:57.780
Wouldn't it be hard to make it float with 
all the food it eats weighing it down?

00:04:57.780 --> 00:04:59.350
Oh, right.

00:04:59.350 --> 00:05:01.820
It sounds hard to eat that much, too.

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:04.810
And if it's a balloon, its movement 
would be dictated by the wind.

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:08.820
Let's switch our approach! 
Maybe the whole thing doesn't have to fly!

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:12.690
We want to make the dragon fly.

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:15.830
So we'll just make a body part 
that looks like a dragon fly.

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:17.790
That's revolutionary!

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:21.250
Only someone with countless designs under their
 belt could come up with something like that!

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:23.100
Oh, it's not all that.

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:26.490
But wouldn't it be a shame if the 
dragon couldn't float by itself?

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:30.110
Then how about making it so that it discards 
that piece and runs away when an enemy comes?

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:32.610
Kin-chan, you're really on fire!

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:37.100
All right, it's done!

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:40.170
Wow, that's more original than I imagined.

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:42.860
What's the dragon part? Is it the tail?

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:48.030
I moved the part that collects the farts out 
and made it into a flotation device.

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:51.470
If it's not big enough, I figured 
the dragon part wouldn't fly,

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:53.110
so I made the main body bigger, too!

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:57.630
So the dragon part is 
basically an abdominal hernia?

00:05:57.630 --> 00:06:01.550
When an enemy comes, it'll cut off 
the dragon part like a lizard.

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:05.640
I see! So it'll escape while using
the dragon is the diversion.

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:09.130
Is it really okay to make this thing?

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:13.190
Do you feel like we're missing 
something about the dragon?

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:15.610
Let's ask the original designer.

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:18.390
Wait, Mizushima's gone. Did he go home?

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:21.560
Maybe this was too far from his beautiful ideal.

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:24.870
He has been influenced quite 
heavily by Tsuchiya-san.

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:26.030
Oh, really?

00:06:26.310 --> 00:06:30.070
Really. That's why the dragon 
has a bit of a horse face.

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:31.690
Oh, I see.

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:36.380
Um, about the dragon's mouth...

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:40.530
Anatomically speaking, 
is that the animal's...

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.140
It's the anus!

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:47.490
I figured. Of course Mizushima-san got mad.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:50.850
But this is just what happened when 
I really tried to make it work.

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:54.100
It's a dream and a sign 
of your growth,

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:57.050
to have a design from your younger days 
reevaluated and accepted.

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:00.830
<i>How serious are these people?</i>

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:06.330
It's so majestic... but it's full of farts.

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:09.580
Anyway, is it okay to cut off 
a part of the body like that?

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:15.560
That's fine! I added a "detach here" feature,
 like lizards have with their tails.

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:18.450
It's like breaking off 
part of a lotus root.

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:21.960
Dropping off the intestines is new.

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:25.410
What's the reasoning behind 
making the body a chicken?

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:28.700
Oh, we wanted to make fire come 
out of the dragon's mouth.

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:29.720
Fire?

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:33.730
We arrived at the solution of having it spew 
 flammable urine that just has to be ignited.

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:37.090
That's why I based it on a bird which has 
a combined anus and urethra.

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:40.370
Isn't it so cool when something 
comes out of the mouth?

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:42.590
No! I mean, "poop" comes out of there, too!

00:07:42.590 --> 00:07:46.270
And flammable urine doesn't 
sound so easy, either.

00:07:47.380 --> 00:07:51.850
That ball was in Mizushima-san's 
original design, too.

00:07:52.230 --> 00:07:53.440
It's a kidney stone!

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:55.730
<i>Poor Mizushima-san.</i>

00:08:02.820 --> 00:08:03.950
What was that?

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:08.110
Just forget about the dragon.

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:12.100
Why did it suddenly explode, though?

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:13.980
That was terrifying.

00:08:13.980 --> 00:08:17.280
Looks like it got hit by 
static electricity and exploded.

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:20.480
It was filled of hydrogen.
 That burns well.

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:23.750
Anyway, what was the thing 
that just flew by?

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:25.970
That seemed like a weird animal.

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:29.180
I thought of an animal 
that flies without wings.

00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:30.490
I came up with this...

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:32.200
A flying snake!

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:33.250
A snake?!

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:36.190
Snakes don't have anything 
that makes them fly, right?

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:37.740
How does it fly?

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:39.530
Let's see it first hand.

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:45.750
It's swimming through the air?!

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.270
But it looks like a normal snake.

00:08:48.270 --> 00:08:50.140
No, it's no ordinary snake.

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:52.760
It's kind of flat?

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:57.750
That's right. When it's gliding, it spreads 
out its ribs to generate more lift.

00:08:57.750 --> 00:09:02.180
It can go up to 100 meters horizontally. 
It can even change direction midflight!

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:03.900
God has spoken!

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:07.400
<b>Flying Snake</b>

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:06.360
Accepted!

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:07.400
<b>Accepted</b>

00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:11.040
This is what real growth looks like. Hmph.

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:12.460
Aw.

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:14.030
<b>Rejected</b>

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:16.530
<b>A Few Days Later—</b>

00:09:15.410 --> 00:09:16.520
God has spoken!

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:19.530
<b>Starfish</b>

00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:18.860
Accepted!

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:19.530
<b>Accepted</b>

00:09:19.730 --> 00:09:22.540
Oh, your star doodle made it?

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:27.550
Yup! The hole that could be its mouth 
or its anus can expel its organs!

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:30.020
We learn from our mistakes.

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:35.550
<b>The Illustrated Guide to Creatures That Really Exist</b>

00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:34.990
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures 
That Really Exist!

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:39.020
So it can regenerate its arms 
and legs when they're cut off.

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:40.510
Which are the arms and which are the legs?

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:41.900
There's no distinction.

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:43.930
No distinction between the 
head and butt, either?

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:47.290
This little one's got the mouth on 
the bottom and the anus on top.

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:48.300
But it depends on the species.

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:51.620
Some poop from their mouths. 
Do you want to hear more?

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:54.860
I'm good for now. 
What's with its organs coming out?

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:57.320
The stomach turns inside out, then jumps out!

00:09:57.560 --> 00:09:59.080
Like this.

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:00.620
How can that be good?!

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:03.470
They grab their prey with their 
stomach and then digest it.

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:06.710
That way, they can eat prey that's 
bigger than their mouth.

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:09.070
Isn't that awesome? I want 
to be like that, too.

00:10:09.070 --> 00:10:11.030
I guess everybody's different.

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:19.430
Tsuchiya-san...

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:24.380
It's about the seahorse, 
where the design passed by itself.

00:10:24.380 --> 00:10:26.300
Ah, what about it?

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:29.650
I believe I submitted both 
male and female designs.

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:33.570
Oh, the little kelpie that was 
submitted with the dolphins.

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:33.440
<b>Accepted</b>

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:33.440
<b>Seahorse</b>

00:10:33.970 --> 00:10:36.390
There's a bit of an issue here.

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:42.200
<b>Father</b>

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:42.200
<b>Mother</b>

00:10:37.390 --> 00:10:41.060
The male and female labels are mixed up.

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:42.200
<b>Female</b>

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:42.200
<b>Male</b>

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:42.200
<b>Accepted</b>

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:44.380
This handwriting...

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:50.090
My name is Tsuchiya Kenta! 
Thank you for taking care of my grandpa!

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:55.450
Hello, Kenta-kun! Would you like a cream puff?

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:56.740
Thank you!

00:10:58.030 --> 00:11:00.270
Anyway, these scribbles...

00:11:00.270 --> 00:11:02.980
They make you sense a frightening future.

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:05.030
Just what I expect from my grandson.

00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:06.980
What are you saying?!

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:09.470
Of course, we'll keep it as-is.

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:13.360
<b>Idiot</b>

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:13.360
<b>Grandpa</b>

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:13.370
I can't allow myself to nip 
a child's talent in the bud!

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:16.480
He's emboldened because the 
design was already accepted.

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:19.280
But having the male be the mother
 and the female be the father

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:21.110
is a fundamental contradiction.

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:22.780
How are you going to resolve this?

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:26.160
Maybe change sexes like clownfish?

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:27.110
You're the reinforcements?

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:32.290
At first, they're all male, but then the 
biggest individual in the school becomes female,

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:35.380
<b>Female</b>

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:35.380
<b>Male</b>

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:35.360
and then the next biggest one becomes her mate.

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:35.380
<b>Immature Individuals</b>

00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:39.400
But isn't that too weak for saying 
that the "male is the mother"?

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:41.910
It's just "the mother was male at first."

00:11:41.910 --> 00:11:42.880
Indeed.

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:45.170
Then how about this?

00:11:45.170 --> 00:11:49.380
Mizushima, can you take over for 
Shimoda-kun and keep Kenta-kun company?

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:53.300
There's a lot we can't 
settle without an angel.

00:11:53.300 --> 00:11:54.800
Oh, right.

00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:56.280
Thank you, Mizushima-kun.

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:58.160
A-All right.

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:06.820
My name is Mizushima. Nice to meet you.

00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:11.340
Do you want some coffee?

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:15.580
<b>Father</b>

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:15.580
<b>Female</b>

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:15.580
<b>Mother</b>

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:15.580
<b>Male</b>

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:15.580
<b>Accepted</b>

00:12:12.590 --> 00:12:15.580
It's male even though it's female, 
and it's female even though it's male.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:19.320
Isn't it a bit like the footballfish 
that was accepted a while ago?

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:21.460
Oh, what's that like?

00:12:22.390 --> 00:12:25.590
The females are way bigger than the males.

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:25.590
<b>Female</b>

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:25.590
<b>Male</b>

00:12:25.980 --> 00:12:31.220
The males approach their beloved female,
 bite her, stick to her,

00:12:31.870 --> 00:12:35.350
melt their bodies, share blood
 vessels with the female,

00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:39.610
melt their brains, and soon
 lose consciousness.

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:44.690
Then they are reduced to nothing but testicles,
 and become organs inside the female!

00:12:44.690 --> 00:12:46.930
Isn't that so romantic?!

00:12:46.150 --> 00:12:49.170
That's scary. Downright terrifying!

00:12:49.170 --> 00:12:51.490
I'm sorry, but you'll have 
to get used to it soon.

00:12:51.490 --> 00:12:54.410
I-I don't think fusing is quite right.

00:12:54.410 --> 00:12:57.530
We have to flip male and female somehow.

00:12:58.230 --> 00:13:01.290
Then maybe we'll have the males give birth.

00:13:01.290 --> 00:13:04.750
I-I feel like I heard some nonsense just now.

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:10.390
<b>Female</b>

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:10.390
<b>Male</b>

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:10.380
We'll add a pouch for offspring to the males,
 and give the female a tube for injecting eggs.

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:14.690
The female inserts the eggs into 
the male's body, and the male...

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:14.980
<b>Suffering</b>

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:15.740
Gives birth!

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:16.400
<b>Birth</b>

00:13:16.660 --> 00:13:19.160
I did it! The male is the mother!

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:22.160
Higuchi-san, let's try that right away!

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:23.650
Yeah, all right...

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:27.020
What happened?

00:13:27.270 --> 00:13:30.160
Well, he said he wanted some coffee.

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:33.160
It's so bitter!

00:13:33.480 --> 00:13:35.450
Even so, why'd you give it to him black?

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:39.820
Kenta-kun, what animals do you like?

00:13:40.370 --> 00:13:41.780
I love horses!

00:13:41.780 --> 00:13:44.160
He is Tsuchiya-san's grandson.

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:48.040
Grandpa made me five of these.

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:51.920
They transform, combine, and become a giant!

00:13:51.920 --> 00:13:53.430
I love this kind of animal!

00:13:57.690 --> 00:14:01.910
All right! Let's make the biggest combining 
life form in the world for Kenta-kun!

00:14:01.910 --> 00:14:03.940
Did you hit your head?

00:14:04.310 --> 00:14:08.460
It just needs to be fine alone,
 but also combined.

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:08.450
m 19 68 l 28 99 68 106 88 101 93 92 67 64 55 59 32 59

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:08.450
<b>I'll be
 the head</b>

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:08.450
m 19 136 l 21 147 29 159 38 167 65 169 76 166 83 159 87 148 68 130 51 124 30 125

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:08.450
<b>I'll be the
right arm</b>

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:08.450
m 94 210 l 99 228 110 239 124 243 144 238 153 232 145 200 131 198 111 199

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:08.450
<b>I'll be the
 right leg</b>

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:08.450
m 493 126 l 493 143 506 164 527 170 540 169 550 165 554 147 548 125 532 120 510 118

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:08.450
<b>I'll be the
 left leg</b>

00:14:06.740 --> 00:14:08.450
m 557 23 l 560 38 568 50 579 55 602 55 610 48 615 38 602 15 584 13 568 15

00:14:06.740 --> 00:14:08.450
<b>I'll be the
 right arm</b>

00:14:17.300 --> 00:14:18.200
Eureka!

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:23.190
Many individuals will gather and arrange 
themselves into a formation that's like a single being.

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:27.720
It'll be a gigantic life form that'll surpass 
even the world's biggest animal, the blue whale!

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:29.720
And it is a jellyfish!

00:14:30.310 --> 00:14:31.470
God has spoken!

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:34.350
<b>Siphonophorae</b>

00:14:31.820 --> 00:14:33.900
Accepted!

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:34.350
<b>Accepted</b>

00:14:35.530 --> 00:14:40.110
Kenta-kun's not crying! 
We might be on the right track here.

00:14:40.590 --> 00:14:43.490
Okay, everyone, will you help me out?

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:45.070
What a silly question.

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:48.110
I'll start with my creation, the snake!

00:14:48.310 --> 00:14:52.120
I'll contribute the bird! 
With wings, anything will be graceful!

00:14:52.330 --> 00:14:56.740
I'll add the anteater. With this one, 
I think it'll add cool claws.

00:14:56.970 --> 00:14:58.980
Then I'll pitch in the sea cucumber.

00:15:00.510 --> 00:15:02.990
Then I'll go for the squid!

00:15:05.330 --> 00:15:06.990
Combine!

00:15:13.840 --> 00:15:15.510
It's an evil god!

00:15:15.510 --> 00:15:17.140
Something unspeakable came out!

00:15:19.300 --> 00:15:20.590
Delete.

00:15:25.780 --> 00:15:28.230
I came here because I had a bad feeling.

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:33.020
You can't make dangerous things like that.

00:15:33.020 --> 00:15:34.840
What if it got accepted?

00:15:34.840 --> 00:15:36.970
Let's seal away that recipe.

00:15:36.970 --> 00:15:38.780
K-Kenta-kun, are you okay?

00:15:39.090 --> 00:15:40.940
It was awesome!

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:42.680
A-Ah, that's a relief.

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:44.910
What was awesome?

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:46.670
Have you finished the seahorse?

00:15:47.020 --> 00:15:50.170
Yes, look. The father's going 
to do his best to give birth!

00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:52.170
God has spoken!

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:54.390
<b>Accepted</b>

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:54.460
Accepted!

00:15:54.740 --> 00:15:58.220
Huh? The seahorse was already accepted.

00:15:58.220 --> 00:15:59.800
So something else?

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:03.920
The jellyfish was accepted, 
and the evil god was sealed away.

00:16:03.920 --> 00:16:05.940
I don't have anything in progress.

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:07.210
Me neither.

00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:08.270
Same.

00:16:08.270 --> 00:16:10.810
Same for me. Then who?

00:16:11.140 --> 00:16:12.070
I did it!

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:16.570
I doodled a lot while 
playing in that room!

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:16.580
<b>Prototype Lab</b>

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:19.080
<b>Prototype Lab</b>

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:23.330
Wh-What kind of animal was accepted?

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:32.810
Close it! Close it!

00:16:34.670 --> 00:16:37.230
Wh-What was that? Did we hallucinate?

00:16:37.230 --> 00:16:39.720
That was super real!

00:16:41.070 --> 00:16:43.780
Make that one work, please.

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:48.490
He just gave up. He's leaving 
it all in your hands.

00:16:48.490 --> 00:16:52.700
What? I thought he accepted it? 
What does he mean, make it work?!

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:54.360
I say he accepted it because of the vibe.

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:56.560
I'm sowwy!

00:16:56.560 --> 00:16:59.000
It's not you! We're just mad at our client.

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:00.360
Oh, there, there.

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:05.110
We can't just leave it in there.

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:08.080
Deleting won't work since it's 
already accepted, right?

00:17:08.310 --> 00:17:10.560
A child's doodle is a frightening thing.

00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:12.380
I'm only frightened of my grandson's talent.

00:17:12.580 --> 00:17:16.180
Why not just seal the entire room with it?

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:19.520
My tools are still in there.

00:17:19.830 --> 00:17:21.610
Mizushima-san, are you one of those people

00:17:21.610 --> 00:17:25.750
who doesn't understand that those 
are my precious treasures?

00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:27.280
I-I'm sorry.

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:30.590
If we can't seal it, 
should we kill it with poison? Can we?

00:17:30.590 --> 00:17:33.290
We can't just kill it! We don't even 
know what kind of animal it is.

00:17:33.560 --> 00:17:36.570
Hm, how about calming it with a tranquilizer?

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:40.540
That's good! Moles and their kin can do that.

00:17:41.020 --> 00:17:43.140
Their saliva contains tranquilizing agents that

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:45.760
put the earthworms they eat 
into suspended animation.

00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:48.040
That's so they can stockpile 
them underground.

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:49.890
That's a good idea.

00:17:49.890 --> 00:17:51.160
Hold on!

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:56.650
To put a creature that size to sleep, 
we'd need to make a 300 meter mole!

00:17:56.650 --> 00:17:59.170
That would definitely only make things worse.

00:17:59.170 --> 00:18:01.490
Isn't there something we can do?

00:18:01.490 --> 00:18:03.950
If only we had the design.

00:18:03.950 --> 00:18:06.680
Kenta, do you remember what you drew?

00:18:09.910 --> 00:18:13.560
Then our only choice is to come up with 
an animal that can get us the design!

00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:16.110
Something strong, dexterous, and robust!

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:19.440
Let's speed it up by tweaking 
something that's already done.

00:18:19.710 --> 00:18:21.880
It should have a strong body, right?

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:24.020
Then how about a gorilla?

00:18:24.520 --> 00:18:26.880
Let's start by making it gigantic.

00:18:34.820 --> 00:18:37.090
Of course. This always happens.

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:38.850
It's heatstroke.

00:18:38.850 --> 00:18:41.710
Why? It's not hot in here.

00:18:41.710 --> 00:18:45.500
When you double body size, 
body volume doesn't just double.

00:18:44.930 --> 00:18:48.230
Heat Pack

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:48.160
Imagine a box with a heat pack in it.

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:50.600
Heat Pack

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:50.600
Heat Pack

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:50.600
Heat Pack

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:50.600
Heat Pack

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:50.590
If you double each side, 
how many heat packs will you get?

00:18:50.590 --> 00:18:54.370
E-Eight... Oh, that's why it's too toasty.

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:56.730
Cells produce heat, too.

00:18:56.740 --> 00:18:59.240
<b>Warm</b>

00:18:56.740 --> 00:19:01.490
<b>Asian Black Bear</b>

00:18:56.740 --> 00:19:06.000
<b>Brown Bear</b>

00:18:56.820 --> 00:19:06.000
<b>Polar Bear</b>

00:18:56.960 --> 00:18:59.920
The bigger the animal is, 
the more heat it produces,

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:01.540
making it better at enduring the cold.

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:04.620
<b>Cold</b>

00:19:01.540 --> 00:19:05.040
That's why animals like bears 
are bigger in colder regions.

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:05.990
Oh, I see!

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:08.200
This isn't the time for chit-chat!

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:10.760
We have to enhance this gorilla fast!

00:19:10.760 --> 00:19:14.010
Shouldn't increasing the surface area 
exposed to air cool it better?

00:19:14.310 --> 00:19:16.410
Like adding big heat sinks.

00:19:16.410 --> 00:19:18.500
That's it! Let's add a comb!

00:19:19.890 --> 00:19:21.880
I think that's not sufficient.

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:24.450
How about shaving it, so it's bald?

00:19:25.070 --> 00:19:28.000
<i>So when it's not a horse, 
he doesn't care what it looks like.</i>

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:31.490
I don't really want to make it all smooth.

00:19:31.490 --> 00:19:33.860
Let's allow him to keep the undies, at least.

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:35.760
I think nothing at all would
 be better than that.

00:19:35.760 --> 00:19:38.020
But completely naked from the get go?

00:19:38.020 --> 00:19:40.280
The gorilla was completely 
naked in the beginning.

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:42.360
Let's add a pattern, then.

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:44.410
And some spikes to make it stronger.

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:46.380
Okay, it's done!

00:19:46.380 --> 00:19:47.920
Oh, it's able to stand.

00:19:50.470 --> 00:19:52.540
Behold, the revised gorilla!

00:19:53.050 --> 00:19:54.780
<i>The world's finished.</i>

00:19:56.480 --> 00:19:57.510
It collapsed!

00:19:57.510 --> 00:19:59.040
Can't go without this.

00:19:59.230 --> 00:20:00.960
Its legs broke.

00:20:00.960 --> 00:20:03.550
Doubling its height made its 
weight go up eight-fold.

00:20:03.550 --> 00:20:04.740
It's just not sturdy enough.

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:07.430
Then let's try making the legs thicker,
 and making it a quadruped.

00:20:08.790 --> 00:20:12.810
It's standing for now, but it seems 
that the heat issue's not solved.

00:20:13.050 --> 00:20:14.780
Should we add more heat sinks?

00:20:14.780 --> 00:20:17.090
It doesn't look like it has 
any of the dexterity needed

00:20:17.090 --> 00:20:18.610
to get the design from the lab, either.

00:20:18.620 --> 00:20:19.810
The undies are weird, too.

00:20:20.090 --> 00:20:23.040
If the body's too heavy and we 
can't stretch the arms or legs,

00:20:23.040 --> 00:20:24.600
why not make the nose longer?

00:20:27.490 --> 00:20:32.250
<b>Elephant</b>

00:20:28.900 --> 00:20:30.440
Yes, it's done!

00:20:30.440 --> 00:20:32.570
Accepted!

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:32.290
<b>Accepted</b>

00:20:33.060 --> 00:20:36.710
It brought us Kenta-kun's design in a flash.

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:39.760
It's smart, it's got a dexterous nose,
 and it's cute!

00:20:39.760 --> 00:20:42.710
Making the ears the heat sink was perfect.

00:20:42.710 --> 00:20:45.530
I like the change from spikes to tusks, too.

00:20:45.530 --> 00:20:47.860
This design is bad news!

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:51.970
I have no idea what kind 
of creature this is!

00:20:51.970 --> 00:20:53.490
It only has the size written on it!

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:58.240
This isn't 30 meters, it's three centimeters!

00:20:58.240 --> 00:20:59.850
No, it's thirty—

00:20:59.850 --> 00:21:02.370
Oh, it was three centimeters.

00:21:02.370 --> 00:21:04.000
You heard him, God!

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:06.610
Okay!

00:21:12.300 --> 00:21:13.640
It's over.

00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:15.870
We've got a cutie now.

00:21:15.870 --> 00:21:19.630
<b>Hallucigenia</b>

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:18.840
Accepted again!

00:21:17.960 --> 00:21:19.630
<b>Accepted</b>

00:21:19.640 --> 00:21:22.160
This has been upside-down the whole time.

00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:26.760
The wavy things are the legs, 
and the thorns are on the back.

00:21:27.010 --> 00:21:28.770
Then what's this black stuff here?

00:21:29.010 --> 00:21:30.320
Poop!

00:21:31.770 --> 00:21:36.270
<b>The Illustrated Guide to Creatures That Really Exist</b>

00:21:32.290 --> 00:21:35.320
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures 
That Really Exist!

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:40.480
Hallucigenia! Its name means 
"creator of hallucinations."

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:43.280
So it's a small marine creature.

00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:46.560
I would have liked to see a big version 
of this stomping around on land.

00:21:46.560 --> 00:21:49.670
Then it would have probably 
had legs like an elephant.

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:54.330
The elephant's the ideal manifestation 
of a large land animal.

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:56.420
The ears are heat sinks, right?

00:21:56.420 --> 00:22:00.800
Instead of panting when it's hot,
 they flap their ears.

00:22:00.990 --> 00:22:02.890
Is there a reason for the wrinkles, too?

00:22:02.890 --> 00:22:06.110
Yes, the wrinkles increase the 
surface area of their bodies,

00:22:06.110 --> 00:22:08.060
which helps shed heat.

00:22:08.250 --> 00:22:10.710
Additionally, they also 
serve to collect rain.

00:22:10.710 --> 00:22:15.050
Oh, so having wrinkles helps 
moisturize their skin!

00:23:45.070 --> 00:23:46.570
<b>Next on the Agenda</b>
